FEATURE: timeline-list-verification
DATE: 2026-10-05
SCOPE: verify the TimeLineList module, fix what is broken, and document it

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The vUX library (this repository). The workspace consumers (Apps/vGet and
Apps/myinvitees/app.myinvitees.com) mount vUX through a symlink and pick up changes on the next
page load. Neither imports vUX-timeLineList.js, so nothing in them changes.

Consumer-visible surface:
  - vUX-timeLineList.js          internals rebuilt around per-instance, per-list classes. The public
                                 API is unchanged. refresh() before autoBuild() or after destroy()
                                 now throws. A second autoBuild() builds newly added lists. The
                                 generated class and sheet ids changed (see ChangeLog 'Changed').
  - assets/css/timeLineList.css  now actually loaded. Adds a 110px label margin (0 when stacked).
                                 Wrap rules moved to three classes.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION METHOD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

There is no test runner, so the module was driven in headless Chromium (chrome-headless-shell) over
a test page served with python3 -m http.server. The checks asserted computed styles (including
::before and ::after), classes, generated stylesheets and thrown messages. The same suite was run
against the original files.

Baseline (original code):   18 passed, 16 failed
After the fixes:            34 passed, 0 failed
Example page suite:         31 passed, 0 failed  (at 1280px and at 375px), plus visual review of
                            screenshots at both widths

The harnesses live in the session scratchpad, not the repository. Not verified: real devices,
or browsers other than Chromium.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 1. autoBuild() threw a SyntaxError ('.vtimeLine[]') without a smallView entry, partway through,
    after marking lists but before binding the resize listener. Every resize threw the same way.
 2. timeLineList.css was never linked, so no markers, no labels and no label column appeared.
 3. Once loaded, the default labels would sit off-screen (no left margin for the column).
 4. Per-list classes vtl0, vtl1… collided across instances, and refresh() reused vtl0 and so on.
 5. refresh() generated no styles for the lists it activated, and did not apply wrap until the
    next resize.
 6. Misspelled guards (…Atrrib) were always true, so "{null}" rules were written for unconfigured
    and missing attributes.
 7. wrapList toggled every .vtimeLine on the page, including other instances' lists.
 8. refresh() worked before autoBuild() (no CSS, no listener) and after destroy() (lists never
    unmarked again). With no className it threw a raw SyntaxError.
 9. The autoBuild() re-entry guard looked up "#v"+className, which never exists, so it never fired.
10. dataAttributes accepted non-string values, half-applied a failing assignment, and its count
    message said 4 for a limit of 5.
11. className accepted ".x" or values with spaces, which failed later as an invalid selector.
12. Typos in error messages: imcomplete, supllied, suported.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KNOWN LIMITATIONS (documented, not changed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 - smallView compares against the window width, not the list's (doc/timeline-list.md, Limits).
 - className matches every element carrying it, including non-list wrappers.
 - Styles are compiled at build time. Changing them needs destroy() and a new instance.
 - The default marker uses font-family: vicon, which vUX does not ship. Plain-text markers
   must override font-family.
 - Stacked labels sit at a fixed offset. A large marker needs padding-left in the label style.
